This repository retains and modifies upstream SillyTavern code and adds the SillyAgent native, core-integrated agent harness. The changes listed here describe the SillyAgent fork as of the modification notice date above; later commits may introduce further modifications.

Major fork-specific changes
--------------------------

1. Native agent harness and tool execution
   - Adds a native backend tool endpoint at /api/agent/tools.
   - Adds a tool registry, tool schemas, toolset and write-permission validation, and a bounded agent tool-call runner.
   - Integrates structured tool calling with the existing SillyTavern generation and conversation flow rather than requiring a browser extension.

2. Persistent memory and automatic capture
   - Adds SQLite-backed event, memory, proposal, and scoped retrieval storage.
   - Integrates user and assistant turn capture with internal SillyTavern lifecycle events, including deduplication and character/chat scoping.
   - Adds deletion and lifecycle guards intended to prevent stale asynchronous requests from silently recreating deleted chat or character data.

3. Background reflection and procedural skills
   - Adds an optional backend reflection worker and provider configuration for an OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint.
   - Adds validation of structured memory/skill candidates and persistent character-scoped procedural skill storage and tools.
   - Reflection is queued by internal events; it requires a configured and enabled provider to run.

4. Roleplay state and built-in tools
   - Adds persistent world, character, and scene state; scene advancement; lore search; and dice tools.
   - Adds native handlers and validation for these tool families.

5. SillyTavern integration and user-facing changes
   - Modifies core startup, server routing, prompt conversion, chat/character lifecycle, and supported generation/tool-calling paths to connect the runtime.
   - Adds and modifies browser UI scripts, styles, and HTML for the SillyAgent integration.
   - Updates default configuration and package metadata where needed by the fork.

6. Tests, workflow, and documentation
   - Adds SillyAgent-specific unit and integration tests.
   - Adds a SillyAgent CI workflow.
   - Adds architecture, installation (including Android Termux), harness, memory/reflection, and procedural-skill documentation.
   - Adds a third-party dependency license inventory in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

